MyGo patch 0012 (VoxtNew): a text area as high as its text shows its
caret in the page around it.

A text area scrolls its caret into view, but only within itself. One as
high as its text (Lines up to what it holds) has nothing of its own to
scroll, so a caret moved past the window's edge, or a selection the app
set there (a Find), stayed out of sight: VoxtNew capped its rules field
at 36 lines and let it scroll inside the page, two scrollbars nested,
for Find to work. Now the caret revealed is also scrolled into view by
the containers around the area when the area has the focus (the user
moves the caret or types) or when the app sets a selection
(SetTextSelection); an edit the app makes to the text of an area that
does not have the focus moves nothing. reveal is split in revealIn,
which shows a box within an element's, and layoutTree reveals the parts
queued while laying out (TestTextAreaRevealsInPage).

